/* func_level_5_8007B4B0 (0x8007B4B0, level_5_artisans_sunny_flight overlay, 476 bytes).
 *
 * Format and draw the flight-level race time at `pos` (units of 1/6 second).
 * Negative time draws the placeholder string (D_8007AA3C) and returns 6.
 * Otherwise formats h:mm:ss (D_8007AA44) or mm:ss (D_8007AA54) into a stack
 * buffer, right-aligns by the string length (9px per glyph), draws it, and
 * for the hour form additionally draws the colon overlay (D_8007AA5C) twice
 * at 1.5x width. Returns the glyph count.
 * Identical body in the five flight-level overlays -> 2,380 bytes when closed.
 *
 * PARKED 2026-08-17 at 13/119 differing insns, LENGTH-EXACT and SHAPE-EXACT:
 * every instruction is now the right opcode in the right position and the
 * residue is a pure register rotation in the divide block. This body is NOT
 * the lowest differing-insn state (the previous park, without the `sign`
 * local, scores 8/119) but it is the structurally correct one -- see below.
 * Rank this park by shape, not by the sweep's differing-insn count (cookbook
 * SS C: the ranking measures the wrong thing when two states differ in shape).
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ROOT CAUSE (2026-08-17), read straight off `cc1 -dS`'s scheduler trace and
 * gcc 2.7.2 `sched.c` / `expmed.c`. Do NOT re-derive; the two knots the
 * 2026-07-16/19/25/26 notes described as "a double reg-permutation knot,
 * permuter-or-hand-asm only" are ONE knot, and it is not a tie.
 *
 * Knot (2) ("`len += 1` deferred into the pos[0] load-delay") is GONE -- the
 * whole tail from 0x8007B580 on is byte-identical. Only the divide block
 * 0x8007B514..0x8007B57C differs.
 *
 * The divide block. The three signed divides (/600 q600, /6, /36000 hr) share
 * ONE `time >> 31` sign correction. `expmed.c expand_divmod` ALWAYS emits the
 * post-shift `t2 = hi >> post_shift` BEFORE the sign `t3 = op0 >> 31` (both
 * arms of the `ml < 2^31` test), so the /600 divide's `sra 6` is created
 * before the sign it shares. The original has them the other way round:
 *
 *     8007B534  sra v1,a0,31   <- sign FIRST
 *     8007B538  sra a0,t1,6    <- then the /600 post-shift
 *
 * Why ours came out reversed, from the `-dS` trace of the base body:
 *   ;; insn[ 60]: priority =   12   (the sra 6)
 *   ;; insn[ 61]: priority =    1   (the sign)
 *   ;; ready list at T-17: 60 (7f000001) 61 (7f000001), now 61 60
 * Both insns are ready at the same step (their only unscheduled consumer, the
 * `subu` that forms q600, is placed at T-16), and both had their priority
 * REWRITTEN to 0x7f000001. That is `sched.c adjust_priority`: an insn with no
 * REG_DEAD notes whose `birthing_insn_p` holds is raised to `max_priority`.
 * `birthing_insn_p` requires `reg_n_sets[dest] == 1`, which is true for both
 * compiler temps -- so the real priorities (12 vs 1, which would have picked
 * the `sra 6` first) are erased and `rank_for_schedule` falls through to its
 * INSN_LUID tiebreak. sched.c schedules BACKWARD and takes ready[0], so the
 * HIGHER LUID is placed LATER: the sign (created second) lands at 0x8007B538.
 *
 * THE LEVER: give the sign a source-level carrier so its insn is created
 * before the /600 divide. A bare `sign = time >> 31;` does NOT work -- it is
 * dead at that point and jump.c deletes it before cse can redirect the
 * divides onto it (measured: byte-identical to omitting it). It survives once
 * the variable has a SECOND set, which the early-return arm supplies for free
 * (`sign = 6; return sign;` is the `li v0,6` the original already emits in the
 * bgez delay slot). With that, the user's shift sits at a low LUID, wins the
 * tiebreak, and the scheduler still places it at 0x8007B534 because that is
 * where its consumers need it. Both `sra`s are now in the original's order.
 *
 * RULED OUT this session, each with a measurement:
 *  - Reordering the divides so a post_shift==0 divide (`/6`, the only one) is
 *    expanded first DOES flip the sign into place for free, but the mult group
 *    order follows source order, so the /6 magic lands first and the whole
 *    tail shifts: 90/119 (`d6` first), 90/119 (single-set `d6`+`cpy` temps),
 *    91/119 (divides interleaved with the frac statement). This retires the
 *    2026-07-16-1 note's framing -- the mult order is not an independent dial,
 *    it is decided by which mfhi consumer the scheduler places deepest.
 *  - The `do { } while (0)` wrapper around the divides (the 2026-07-26-2
 *    permuter finding) is worth 5 insns on the OLD body (8/119 vs 13/119
 *    without) but +13 on the corrected shape (26/119) -- it was compensating
 *    for the wrong schedule, not causing the right one.
 *  - Copy direction is not a dial: `q600 = time/600; frac = q600;`,
 *    `frac = time/600; q600 = frac;` and two independent `time/600` divides
 *    all give the identical 13/119.
 *
 * REMAINING RESIDUE (pure allocation, 13 insns):
 *      value       orig   ours
 *      sign        v1     a0
 *      mfhi /600   t1     v1
 *      q600 def    a0     a3
 *      q600 copy   a3     v1
 *      min         v0     v1
 * `local-alloc.c qty_compare_1` ranks quantities by
 * `floor_log2(n_refs)*n_refs / (death - birth)`, ties -> lower qty number.
 * Ours packs three values into v1 where the original spreads them and pushes
 * the /600 mfhi out to t1. The single decision to reverse: our `mfhi /600`
 * quantity takes v1 over the sign's range, so the sign (allocated first, 4
 * refs over ~14 insns) falls through to a0 -- the register `time` just
 * vacated. In the base body the sign is a compiler temp and DOES land in v1,
 * so v1 is reachable; making it a user variable is what moves it.
 * NEXT: run the SS D 2c `-dl`/`-dg` probe (dispositions for this body are
 * pseudo 80 = sign in 4, 75 = q600 in 3, 77 = min in 3, 78 = frac in 7) and
 * buy/sell refs (A194/A195) to get the sign allocated ahead of the /600 mfhi,
 * or find a second-set carrier that keeps the sign a SINGLE-BLOCK quantity
 * (the early-return arm makes it span two blocks). Do not aim the permuter at
 * this -- it is arithmetic, not a tie.
 */

extern void func_80017FE4(); /* draw text run */
extern void func_80062FD4(); /* sprintf */
extern int func_8006276C();  /* strlen */

int func_level_5_8007B4B0(int time, int *pos, int arg2)
{
  char buf[16];
  int q600;
  int hr;
  int min;
  int frac;
  int len;
  int sign;

  if (time < 0)
  {
    pos[0] -= 0x36;
    pos[1] -= 5;
    func_80017FE4("......", pos, 0x12, arg2);
    sign = 6;
    return sign;
  }

  sign = time >> 31;
  q600 = time / 600;
  frac = time / 600;
  frac = (time / 6) - (frac * 100);
  hr = time / 36000;
  min = q600 - (hr * 60);

  if (hr != 0)
  {
    func_80062FD4(buf, "%d %02d.%02d", hr, min, frac);
  }
  else
  {
    func_80062FD4(buf, "%d.%02d", min, frac);
  }
  len = func_8006276C(buf);
  pos[0] -= len * 9;
  func_80017FE4(buf, pos, 0x12, arg2);
  if (hr != 0)
  {
    char *fmt = ".";
    pos[0] -= 0x6C;
    pos[1] += 1;
    pos[2] = (pos[2] * 3) >> 1;
    func_80017FE4(fmt, pos, 0x12, arg2);
    len += 1;
    pos[0] -= 0x12;
    pos[1] -= 8;
    func_80017FE4(fmt, pos, 0x12, arg2);
  }
  return len;
}
